        <!-- v11.0.0 (2026-09-21): VISUAL MATURITY pass on the approved v9/v10
             geometry. Footprints unchanged: left zone (6,10 480x940), console
             rail (486,24 76x912), hero 520px at (900,430), prev (900,10) /
             next (900,850), title beneath hero, footer.
             What changed is the treatment:
               - left zone: no single white card. Three layered modules with
                 breathing room between them (the Nova background shows
                 through): a masthead plate holding the marquee, an editorial
                 metadata sheet with a royal-blue spine, a print module for
                 the screenshot. Asymmetric silhouettes, architectural blue
                 corners, faint blueprint, halftone edges, paper grain,
                 refined baked shadows.
               - marquee: a real masthead - navy well baked into the plate,
                 tracked "NOW SHOWING" kicker, full-opacity art, breathing
                 room, a short restrained yellow strike.
               - metadata: editorial order - short description FIRST, one
                 large anchor stat (the marker year), then grouped facts with
                 tracked small-caps kickers (genre / players / developer /
                 rating). Hairline rule, no settings-menu styling.
               - screenshot: a print module - punched window, blue pinstripe,
                 tracked caption baked into the lip, yellow tick.
               - hero: tighter asymmetric blue atmosphere, crisper contact
                 shadow, ONE restrained gold rim-light arc on the lower-left
                 silhouette. The yellow halo stays retired.
               - neighbours: dimmed hard (0.55/0.6/0.45), real media objects.
               - title: double rule (white hairline + yellow bar), marker
                 display face, white. Rule at 716, title at 736, unchanged.
             v10 assets retired: lib_panel, lib_marquee_back, lib_strike_yellow,
             lib_shot_frame, lib_rule_yellow (superseded by the modules).
             Verified against ES-DE v3.4.1: vertical carousel pitch =
             element height / maxItemCount = 1260/3 = 420px; scissor clips
             the partially off-screen neighbours. Motion: native eased
             carousel transitions only. -->

